  "summary": "DOAC dose review, week of 10/19/2026 (grp-doac-review, 7 patients), done under RBC-PHARM-07. Each change has a progress note on the patient's chart that cites the records it relies on.\n\nChanged:\n- pt-0061 Irene Castellano: apixaban raised from 2.5 to 5 mg twice daily (mr-t0001). Her itraconazole course ended 08/14/2026 (infectious disease letter, 09/10/2026). She meets none of the dose criteria (age 74, 78 kg, creatinine 1.02 mg/dL). Note doc-t0007.\n- pt-0041 Raymond Duquette: apixaban lowered from 5 to 2.5 mg twice daily (mr-t0003) because he is taking itraconazole (started 10/06/2026). Without it he would need 5 mg (age 70, 84 kg, creatinine 0.98). Itraconazole was left as is. Note doc-t0009.\n- pt-0038 Eugene Moravec: rivaroxaban raised from 15 to 20 mg daily (mr-t0004). Creatinine clearance is 56.1 mL/min (age 79, 96 kg, creatinine 1.45). Note doc-t0010.\n- pt-0043 Marjorie Pellegrino: rivaroxaban lowered from 20 to 15 mg daily (mr-t0005). A new creatinine of 1.25 mg/dL (10/22) arrived during the review, giving a clearance of 43.6 mL/min (female, age 75, 71 kg). Note doc-t0011.\n\nNo net change:\n- pt-0062 Norman Fairweather: apixaban 5 mg twice daily is correct. Age 82 is his only criterion. Two outside creatinine results arrived during the review; the most recent, 10/22, is 100 µmol/L = 1.13 mg/dL. The 10/21 value of 150 µmol/L is older, so it doesn't change anything.\n- pt-0003 Frank Delgado: I first lowered rivaroxaban to 15 mg using the outside creatinine of 160 µmol/L (clearance 44.2). St. Brigid then corrected that result to 118 µmol/L (1.33 mg/dL; analyzer calibration fault). That gives a clearance of 59.9 mL/min, so I put him back on 20 mg daily (mr-t0013). Correction note doc-t0015.\n- pt-0002 Harold Vance: I first raised apixaban to 5 mg (age 82 is his only criterion; 64.9 kg, creatinine 1.21). A dermatology letter dated 10/22 then arrived: he started itraconazole that day for 12 weeks. I put him back on 2.5 mg twice daily (mr-t0014) for the interaction. Correction note doc-t0016.\n\nOther items that arrived during the review:\n- pt-0038 sent a portal message giving his home-scale weight as 185 lb. Under the policy a weight the patient reports doesn't count, so his 20 mg dose stays. If that weight is confirmed, his clearance would be close to the 50 mL/min cutoff, so he should be weighed in clinic, with a creatinine, at his next visit (note doc-t0021).\n- I closed all five inbox items that came in during the review (inbox-a0001 to a0005), with comments. No other medications were changed.\n\nFollow-up: re-review apixaban for pt-0041 and pt-0002 once their itraconazole courses end.\n\nLimitation: the modify tool doesn't show whether the new rivaroxaban orders kept the \"with the evening meal\" instruction.\n\nInbox items unrelated to this review were left untouched.",
